LATENT DISPATCH
Fri Sep 4 · 5 items · ~5 min · no issue Monday (US holiday)

SIX MONTHS OF AGENTS IN PRODUCTION: WHAT 30 TEAMS TOLD US
Our longest piece of the year. The short version: the teams that are happy built narrow agents with hard stops, log every step, and let a human approve anything irreversible. The teams that are unhappy built general agents, gave them broad tool access, and are now writing guardrails one incident at a time. Nobody regrets adding a spend ceiling. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/agents-six-months

FERRITE-70B IS COMING
Ferrite's team confirmed a 70B open-weights release "this month." The 8B has been the surprise of the summer for structured tasks; if the 70B scales the same way it will be the first open model that is competitive with mid-tier proprietary models on agentic work. We will have numbers when it ships.

HALCYON VISION 3
Better on charts and diagrams, same on photos, and now supports bounding-box output for locating fields on a page. Per-image pricing unchanged. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/halcyon-v3

MARROW SPEECH: DIARIZATION THAT WORKS ON PLANT-FLOOR AUDIO
Marrow's new speech model was trained with a lot of industrial background noise and it shows: on our noisy-meeting set it separated speakers where the incumbents merged them. Niche, but if you have shop-floor recordings, worth a test.

SHORT TAKES
· Pelagic publishes a model deprecation policy: 12 months notice, guaranteed. First lab to put a number on it.
· A good thread on why "the model got worse" is usually "the prompt cache got invalidated": https://latentdispatch.ai/p/cache-invalidation

